    "# 04 — System Identification\n",
    "## Learning the Dynamics from Data: DMD, A-Matrix, and Model Drift\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "**The question this module answers:**\n",
    "\n",
    "> *What is the dynamical law governing the latent trajectory? And does it stay the same throughout the recording?*\n",
    "\n",
    "In Modules 2-3, we had *trajectories*. Now we ask: what generates them? The answer is a **linear dynamical system** fit to the data:\n",
    "$$z_{t+1} \\approx A z_t$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why this matters for BCI:**\n",
    "Every decoder that degrades over weeks is a system identification failure. The A matrix you fit in session 1 stops describing the dynamics by session 5 — because the biology drifts. The solution is online system identification: continuously update the model as the data changes.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why this matters for the project:**\n",
    "The eigenvalues of A are the fingerprint of the dynamical regime. We hypothesize:\n",
    "- During 2-back maintenance: eigenvalues near unit circle (stable attractor)\n",
    "- During target detection: eigenvalues temporarily depart (transient destabilization)\n",
    "- Across conditions: eigenvalue structure changes systematically with WM load\n",
    "\n",
    "**Read before this module:**\n",
    "- Brunton & Kutz — *Data-Driven Science and Engineering* — Ch. 7 (DMD)\n",
    "- Proctor, Brunton & Kutz (2016) — *DMDc* — SIAM (in reading list folder likely)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
