    "---\n",
    "## 1. Dynamic Mode Decomposition (DMD)\n",
    "\n",
    "**DMD finds the best-fit linear operator A such that $Z' \\approx A Z$.**\n",
    "\n",
    "Given a trajectory $z_1, z_2, \\ldots, z_T$ (T time points, d dimensions):\n",
    "- Build $Z  = [z_1 | z_2 | \\ldots | z_{T-1}]$ — columns are states\n",
    "- Build $Z' = [z_2 | z_3 | \\ldots | z_T  ]$ — columns are next states\n",
    "- Solve: $A = Z' Z^+$ where $Z^+$ is the pseudoinverse (least squares)\n",
    "\n",
    "**The eigenvalues of A** tell you:\n",
    "- Their magnitude: is the mode decaying ($|\\lambda| < 1$), growing ($|\\lambda| > 1$), or persistent ($|\\lambda| = 1$)?\n",
    "- Their angle: at what frequency does this mode oscillate?\n",
    "- Mapping to Hz: $f = \\angle(\\lambda) \\times \\text{srate} / (2\\pi)$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "dmd-implementation",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def fit_dmd(Z, truncation=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Standard DMD: find A such that Z' ≈ A Z.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Steps:\n",
    "    1. SVD of Z: Z = U Σ Vᵀ (truncate to top r modes)\n",
    "    2. Project into low-dim space: Ã = Uᵀ Z' V Σ⁻¹\n",
    "    3. Eigendecompose Ã → eigenvectors W, eigenvalues λ\n",
    "    4. Lift back to full space: Φ = Z' V Σ⁻¹ W  (DMD modes)\n",
    "\n",
    "    WHY truncated SVD: Avoids noise amplification in pseudoinverse.\n",
    "    The r largest singular values capture the signal; the rest are noise.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        Z          : (d, T-1) — columns are state vectors\n",
    "        truncation : None = keep all, int = keep top-r modes\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns dict:\n",
    "        A      : (d, d) full transition matrix\n",
    "        eigs   : (r,) eigenvalues\n",
    "        modes  : (d, r) DMD modes (spatial patterns)\n",
    "        A_tilde: (r, r) reduced transition matrix\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Z_now  = Z[:, :-1]   # (d, T-1)\n",
    "    Z_next = Z[:, 1:]    # (d, T-1)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Step 1: SVD\n",
    "    U, s, Vt = np.linalg.svd(Z_now, full_matrices=False)\n",
    "    r = truncation if truncation else len(s)\n",
    "    U, s, V  = U[:, :r], s[:r], Vt[:r].T\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Step 2: Project\n",
    "    A_tilde = U.T @ Z_next @ V @ np.diag(1.0 / s)  # (r, r)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Step 3: Eigendecompose reduced A\n",
    "    eigs, W = np.linalg.eig(A_tilde)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Step 4: Lift to full space\n",
    "    Phi = Z_next @ V @ np.diag(1.0 / s) @ W  # (d, r) — DMD modes\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Reconstruct full A\n",
    "    A_full = U @ A_tilde @ U.T  # approximate (only valid in U subspace)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return {'A': A_full, 'eigs': eigs, 'modes': Phi, 'A_tilde': A_tilde}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example: fit DMD to latent trajectory of one trial\n",
    "# Replace with actual mu_np loaded from Module 2:\n",
    "# trial_traj = mu_np[0].T   # (latent_dim, n_times)\n",
    "# dmd_result = fit_dmd(trial_traj, truncation=6)\n",
    "# print('Eigenvalues:', dmd_result['eigs'][:5])\n",
    "# print('|λ|:', np.abs(dmd_result['eigs'])[:5])\n",
    "\n",
    "print('DMD function defined.')"
   ]
  },
