    "---\n",
    "## 2. Online System Identification — Tracking Model Drift\n",
    "\n",
    "**The BCI problem:** In real BCI applications, the decoder is fit at session start and applied throughout. But the brain changes — synaptic weights shift, electrode impedances drift, the patient's strategy adapts. By session end, the model no longer fits the data.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The solution:** **Recursive Least Squares (RLS)** with a forgetting factor λ:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$A_{t+1} = A_t + K_t(z_{t+1} - A_t z_t)^\\top$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $K_t$ is the Kalman gain, and the forgetting factor $\\lambda \\in (0.9, 0.99)$ downweights old observations.\n",
    "\n",
    "**For the N-back data:** Does the A matrix estimated in the 0-back block still describe the 2-back block? If not — that's a scientific result about how dynamics change with WM load. And it's a practical problem for any BCI that needs to work across task conditions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "rls",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class RecursiveLeastSquares:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    RLS for online estimation of A in z_{t+1} = A z_t.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Forgetting factor lambda: 0 = only current sample, 1 = equal weight all samples.\n",
    "    Typical range: 0.95-0.99 for slowly drifting systems.\n",
    "\n",
    "    WHY forgetting factor: Past data becomes less relevant as the system drifts.\n",
    "    Setting lambda = 0.99 means the effective memory length is ~1/(1-lambda) = 100 samples.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    def __init__(self, n_dims, forgetting=0.99):\n",
    "        self.A       = np.eye(n_dims)           # initial estimate\n",
    "        self.P       = np.eye(n_dims) * 100     # covariance matrix (high initial uncertainty)\n",
    "        self.forgetting = forgetting\n",
    "\n",
    "    def update(self, z_now, z_next):\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        Update estimate given one (z_now, z_next) pair.\n",
    "        Returns: updated A (copy)\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        z  = z_now.reshape(-1, 1)\n",
    "        zp = z_next.reshape(-1, 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Prediction error\n",
    "        e = zp - self.A @ z\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Kalman gain\n",
    "        K = self.P @ z / (self.forgetting + z.T @ self.P @ z)\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Update\n",
    "        self.A = self.A + K @ e.T\n",
    "        self.P = (self.P - K @ z.T @ self.P) / self.forgetting\n",
    "\n",
    "        return self.A.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Template: track A over time and monitor |λ_max| as a stability indicator\n",
    "# After loading mu_np:\n",
